ur household has been intrigued by it. I'd recommend it for most viewers who liked the original movie and/or want a different take on the vampire mythos. (Sidenote: El Rey is also *the* go-to channel for chop-socky whoop-ass movies: I don't get to watch it often enough, but it's a hoot to watch the numerous old chop-socky flicks on there -- good times! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T05:59:48-07:00","id":128175,"title":"","content":"Good show, I get El Rey through Time Warner here in Los Angeles, its Robert Rodriguez's own cable network and features alot of kung-fu, martial arts, blaxploitation and other action films, very similar to SPIKE network (caters to males). The channel line up will be showing 3 John Carpenter films and an interview wtih Carpenter himself. From Dusk Till Dawn is the flagship TV show and its getting picked up for a 2nd season.<br /> <br /> My impressions of the show so far are good, really goes into the mythology of Satanico Pandemonium (the Queen vampire) and the &quot;lords of the Night' that created her in ancient times. Cast is solid, good acting and scripting. However, Sex Machine's character concept was changed from the movies, he's more of a supernatural scholar/hunter. Rodriguez said he's envisioned a larger story arc with possible 5 seasons.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Assistant Organizer for:</b><br /> <a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i162.photobucket.com/albums/t261/jlburgos_bucket/a41e98d1-1eed-4506-a8d2-2b3bea4a43da_zps469395ad.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/311-joeb","name":"JoeB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar311_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T06:41:56-07:00","id":128194,"title":"","content":"So far I've only seen the first two episodes (first being the pilot) and though ovbiously different, it looks cool. Seth is almost as I remeber him from the movie, the gestures, the way he talks, everything is almost a perfect match, to the point I forget at time he's not clooney.<br /> <br /> EDIT: seen most of it, save the 2 last ones. Well, Seth seems a bit softer than in the movies and I didn't expect some things that happened between some characters, but so far, so good<br /> <br /> And Seth's pistol is bitchin'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 05-08-2014, 05:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T10:48:25-07:00","id":132420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_conta